<title>FRANCE: Accor 1996 sales slip to 28.31 bln Ffr.</title>
<headline>Accor 1996 sales slip to 28.31 bln Ffr.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of French francs)</p>
<p>    Turnover					28,305    vs   31,012</p>
<p>     of which hotels			    15,931    vs   14,017</p>
<p>     services to companies		     8,434    vs    7,787</p>
<p>     other activities			    3,940    vs    4,320</p>
<p>     Eurest (sold in 1995)		     none     vs    4,888</p>
<p>NOTE - Accor said in a statement that turnover would have risen 2.9 percent at constant structure and exchange rates. Turnover rose 8.3 percent in 1996 excluding Eurest, which it sold on October 1, 1995, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
